{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/capability-consolidation-pilot-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"1f0e5140-a53b-4d6d-9fcc-00464e0d824a","parentId":"63574cf4-f4ff-4d07-adb6-f3560224d70e","name":"Deduplication & type coercion transforms","details":"Build the first half of the cleaning layer: remove duplicate rows and records, then coerce fields to their declared types.

Specifically: define the dedup key per entity (e.g. customer_id + provider + snapshot date), resolve duplicates deterministically (latest arrival wins, with the previous value retained for audit), trim/normalize whitespace and casing on keys, and coerce numerics/booleans with explicit handling of blanks and sentinel values like "N/A".

Unit-test each rule with fixture cases. Keep date/timezone work and PII masking out of this task.","priority":9,"complexity":3,"estimatedHours":12,"tags":["csv","transforms","data-quality"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/capability-consolidation-pilot-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"1f0e5140-a53b-4d6d-9fcc-00464e0d824a","parentId":"63574cf4-f4ff-4d07-adb6-f3560224d70e","name":"Date/timezone normalization & PII masking","details":"Second half of the cleaning layer.

Dates: parse the several date formats identified in the M1 contract, resolve ambiguous day/month ordering per provider, and normalize everything to UTC with the source timezone recorded. Reject or flag dates that are unparseable or implausible (future, pre-2000).

PII: classify columns from the contract, apply masking or hashing per policy, and ensure no raw PII lands in analytics-facing tables. Add tests asserting the masked output for each PII column type.","priority":9,"complexity":4,"estimatedHours":14,"tags":["csv","transforms","pii","privacy"]}

{"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/capability-consolidation-pilot-20261102/cells/cell-005/run/workspace","projectId":"1f0e5140-a53b-4d6d-9fcc-00464e0d824a","parentId":"63574cf4-f4ff-4d07-adb6-f3560224d70e","name":"Incremental load with idempotent upserts","details":"Persist cleaned CSVs into the customer tables using an incremental strategy.

